WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
The night before he
died, at a Passover meal,

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.270
Jesus took bread, gave
thanks for it, and broke it.

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.710
He said: Take, eat; this is my body.

4
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.670
Today, Christians share bread
and wine under many names.

5
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.690
Mass.

6
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.970
Holy Communion.

7
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.630
The Lord's Supper.

8
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.020
So is the bread at Communion
really Jesus' body,

9
00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.370
a reminder of him, or
something in between?

10
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.450
In this mission, you'll
step inside a Catholic Mass,

11
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.300
and meet a long word: transubstantiation.

12
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:37.560
Then you'll weigh up how important
this meal is in Christian worship.

13
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.770
Your mission: find out what different
Christians believe the bread at Communion

14
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.450
is.
